                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237236687",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197998817967",
                            "num_reviews": 333,
                            "playtime_forever": 230,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 230,
                            "last_played": 1381424155
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Over a decade in, this one's mechanics with cuttable physical objects still feel surprisingly fresh.\n\nOverall, while positioning as a puzzle game this one doesn't offer many distinct puzzles to solve, it's best looked at as a physics sandbox a-la Gmod or something, but with a goal, it can all be managed very freeform with a variety to approaches. It's just that fun to slice rocks and then attach rocket thrusters to them.\n\nIt's a short game but you can always get it on sale. Check out the soundtrack too, it's pretty great and eclectic.",
